    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1321">

                <pb facs="1139" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/321</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of
                            State for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        British Ambassador in NT Washington</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spring Rice</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-29">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 29, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received in the Department of State August
                        29</hi>.] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Government have no objection whatever to an arrangement under
                    American control to use any ship for the purpose <pb facs="1140" n="826"
                        xml:id="pg826"/> to which it is proposed to put the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Prince Joachim</hi>. On the contrary, they would readily and gratefully
                    agree to such a plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Grey</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
